    "sections": [
      {
        "name": "PATIENT_INFORMATION",
        "heading": "PATIENT INFORMATION",
        "text": "Patient Name: Rohan Iyer\nPatient Identifier: NEW-PATIENT-001 (External Synthetic ID)\nDate of Birth: 17-Nov-1997 (Age: 26)\nGender: Male\nBlood Group: At\nCLINICAL INFORMATION\nOrdering Physician: Dr. Meenakshi Subramaniam, DM Neurology\nClinical Indication: Recurrent headaches of approximately four months\nduration with migrainous features. Evaluation to exclude\nsecondary intracranial pathology.\nRelevant History: No prior neuroimaging. Neurological examination\nunremarkable per referring clinician.\nTECHNIQUE\nMRI of the brain was performed on a 3.0 Tesla scanner (Siemens MAGNETOM Vida)\nusing the following sequences:\n- Sagittal Tl-weighted\n- Axial Tl-weighted (pre- and post-gadolinium)\n- Axial T2-weighted\n- Axial FLAIR (Fluid-Attenuated Inversion Recovery)\n- Axial DWI (Diffusion-Weighted Imaging) with ADC map\n- Axial SWI (Susceptibility-Weighted Imaging)\n- Coronal T2-weighted\n- Post-contrast axial and coronal Tl-weighted\nIntravenous gadolinium-based contrast agent (Gadovist 0.1 mmol/kg) was\nadministered. No adverse reaction to contrast was observed,",
        "start": 401,
        "end": 1459
      },
      {
        "name": "FINDINGS",
        "heading": "FINDINGS",
        "text": "CEREBRAL HEMISPHERES:\nNo focal parenchymal signal abnormality identified. Grey-white matter\ndifferentiation is well preserved. No areas of restricted diffusion on DWI\nto suggest acute infarction. No evidence of haemorrhagic transformation.\nPOSTERIOR FOSSA:\nCerebellum, brainstem, and fourth ventricle appear normal. No mass or\nsignal abnormality.\nVENTRICULAR SYSTEM:\nLateral ventricles are symmetric and normal in size and configuration.\nThird and fourth ventricles are normal. No hydrocephalus.\nMIDLINE STRUCTURES:\nNo midline shift. Septum pellucidum is midline. Corpus callosum is normal\nin morphology and signal.\nEXTRA-AXIAL SPACES:\nNo extra-axial fluid collection. Sulcal spaces are age-appropriate.\nNo subdural or epidural haemorrhage.\nSELLA / PITUITARY:\nPituitary gland is normal in size and morphology. No sellar or suprasellar\nmass. Optic chiasm is unremarkable.\nORBITS:\nGlobes and extraocular muscles appear normal bilaterally. No retrobulbar\nMass or abnormal enhancement.\nVASCULAR STRUCTURES:\nMajor intracranial vessels demonstrate normal flow voids. No evidence of\naneurysm, arteriovenous malformation, or venous sinus thrombosis on SWI\nand post-contrast sequences.\nPOST-CONTRAST:\nNo abnormal parenchymal or meningeal enhancement following gadolinium\nadministration.\nCALVARIUM AND SCALP:\nNormal. No osseous lesion.\nINCIDENTAL FINDINGS:\nMild mucosal thickening in the right maxillary sinus (likely incidental\ninflammatory change). No other incidental findings of clinical\nsignificance.",
        "start": 1467,
        "end": 2964
      },
      {
        "name": "IMPRESSION",
        "heading": "IMPRESSION",
        "text": "1. No acute intracranial abnormality identified.\n2. No acute infarction, intracranial haemorrhage, or significant mass\neffect.\n3. No space-occupying lesion. No abnormal enhancement.\n4. Normal MRI of the brain.\n5. Incidental mild right maxillary sinus mucosal thickening — likely\nclinically insignificant.\nRECOMMENDATION:\nClinical correlation recommended. The imaging findings do not explain the\npatient's headache symptoms. Further management at the discretion of the\nreferring clinician.\nRADIOLOGIST SIGNATURE\nReported by:\nDr. Ashwin Kulkarni, MD Radiology\nSenior Consultant Radiologist\nSanjeevan Neurosciences Clinic — Diagnostic Imaging Centre, Bengaluru\nDate: 25-Jul-2024\nVerified by:\nDr. Sunita Rao, MD DNB Radiology\nHead, Department of Diagnostic Imaging\nDISCLAIMER: This report is based on the imaging findings at the time of\nexamination and should be interpreted in conjunction with the clinical\nhistory and findings of the treating physician.\nSanjeevan Neurosciences Clinic — Diagnostic Imaging Centre\nPage 1 of 1",
        "start": 2974,
        "end": 3997
      }
    ],
